    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This private compatibility module only declares the legacy resource and\n selector address shapes; it has no handwritten executable code. Its derived\n serialization and identity operations do not emit source-line measurements.\n The source-tool argument and delivery regressions in `agent/tests.rs`\n exercise these addresses through the legacy adapter. Supported path-based\n address construction is tested separately in `tests/outline_content.rs`."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/resource.rs` (root) gives a substantive reason, and the current source and callers support it.\n\n- **No handwritten code:** `struct[ResourceId]` and `struct[OutlineId]` are the only items. Both are plain data structs with derived `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize`. There is no executable code of the file's own to measure.\n- **Private module:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/lib.rs` declares it as `mod resource;`, so it is private.\n- **Regressions through the legacy adapter:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/sources.rs` builds `OutlineId` and deserializes `ResourceId` in `fn[dispatch]`. The tests in `agent/tests.rs` use these types: `fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]` and `fn[source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads]` check what the source tools forward and deliver.\n- **Path-based construction:** `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[addresses_reconstruct_without_reading_the_file]` and `fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` test the supported path-based addresses (`OutlineData`).\n\nThe commentary is in fenced citation commentary, as the built-in requires. It does not claim to excuse any function. The citation is a file-level exception, which is the permitted form.",
